		(property "Note" "2.2k/2.2k, not 10k/10k. The feedback resistor's current (about 44 uA) returns into this node, and 10k/10k's 5k source impedance would move VR_BIAS 220 mV when the output switches -- comparable to the whole hysteresis window. It is a COMMON-MODE shift, so it cancels in the comparison, but it is not worth relying on cancellation for 0.75 mA of quiescent current."
